I gave circuits.com a schema score of **45 / 100**. The homepage markup is fine, but the markup on the Job Board breaks Google's rules, and company profile pages only get schema if JavaScript runs.

The live pages are identical to the files on `main`, so I checked the source directly. The plugin's own page parser wouldn't work through this sandbox's network setup, so I pulled the structured data out with curl and a short script. I couldn't reach Supabase from here, so the markup that `jobs.html` and `profile.js` add after loading data was checked from the code, not from a rendered page.

| Where | Type | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Organization + WebSite (with site search) | ✅ Valid. Organization is thin: no contact point, `sameAs` or founders |
| `/jobs` | Up to 50 JobPosting, added by JS | ❌ Breaks Google's rules |
| `/<handle>` profiles | Organization, added by JS only | ⚠️ Valid, but missed if the page's data fetch fails |
| Other pages | none | No BreadcrumbList anywhere |

No Microdata, RDFa or retired types (HowTo, FAQPage and so on) are in use.

**Fix first:**
1. **Delete the JobPosting code at `jobs.html:141-152` (critical).** Google allows JobPosting only on a page about one job, and putting it on a list page can get the site a manual penalty. It has other errors too:
   - every job's link is `/jobs?q=<keyword>`, so several jobs share a URL;
   - every job is marked `FULL_TIME`, whatever it really is;
   - the location is free text instead of a proper address;
   - the company link points to a circuits.com profile that currently returns 404.

   Bring it back once each job has its own `/jobs/<id>` page. This matches H2 in today's full audit.
2. **Put profile schema into the page HTML (high).** `tools/build-profiles.js` should write ProfilePage + Organization + BreadcrumbList into each generated page. Then the `jsonLd()` function in `profile.js` can go. This depends on fixing the profile generator first (C1 and C2 in the full audit).
3. **Review ratings, for later (medium).** Buyer reviews are switched off, so no rating is output today. If they come back, the code will output a rating with no individual reviews behind it. Add those reviews to the schema when you switch them back on.
4. **Fill out the homepage Organization (low).** Add an email and contact point, and founders if you want them named. `contact.html` can hide Mike's card, so decide whether to name him before adding him.

I didn't recommend FAQPage or HowTo, because Google no longer shows rich results for either. A schema list on `/results` would do nothing until those pages show their listings without JavaScript.

I haven't changed any site code. Both files below are new and uncommitted. In the JSON, anything in `[brackets]` is a fact only you can supply, and you should strip the keys starting with an underscore before using it. Edits to the site still need `node tools/stamp.js` and `node tools/check.js`.

Files are in `seo-reports`:
- 2026-11-10-schema.md
- 2026-11-10-generated-schema.json

